TEXTURES

For the texture manager to be able to understand them,
all textures must be stored as `.png` files.

The general unit to pixel ratio should be 1 to 16.
This ratio may still change in the future, but for
now 1 to 16 seems like a good compromise between
detail and pixelartiness.

Also, all textures should be purely black and white.
During post processing, color might be added, but the
textures themselves should be as simple as possible.
I may decide that grayscale will also be allowed some
day, but never color.
This also has the advantage of smaller file sizes.
